# DECSTBM sets the scrolling region's top and bottom rows and moves the
# cursor home. An omitted or zero top is the first row and an omitted or
# zero bottom the last. A region whose top is not above its bottom is
# ignored, and a bottom past the screen is its last row. CSI ? 1 r is
# XTRESTORE, not DECSTBM, so the region stays.
# spec: the VT510 manual, DECSTBM; ctlseqs, XTRESTORE
# covers: ctl.decstbm
size 10 6
send "\e[2;4r"
dump state
send "\e[4;2r"
dump state
send "\e[2;9r"
dump state
send "\e[3r"
dump state
send "\e[;3r"
dump state
send "\e[0;0r"
dump state
send "\e[3;4H\e[2;5r"
dump state
send "\e[?1r"
dump state
send "\e[r"
dump state
